Subject: Clang driver optional Cosmopolitan libc and Fat-APE support
Upstream-Base: llvmorg-20.1.8 (87f0227cb60147a26a1eeb4fb06e3b505e9c7261)
Fil-C-Head: cede3de02b42b58a14acc9ce39c9894ab952a915 (branch deluge)

Optional patch group layered on top of 06a-clang-driver-filc-core.patch.
Adds Cosmopolitan libc detection (--filc-cosmo), APE/Fat-APE link and
aarch64 shadow-compile orchestration (--filc-ape, --filc-fat-ape,
--filc-no-ape, Command::SoftFail), and aarch64 x18/x28 reservation in
cosmo mode. Not required for Linux or Unikraft builds.

Fil-C-Origin-Commits (7):
  b2dd07be1dd5305de04bdc97f13fd4f2a085b885 2026-10-06 Make Peregrine Fil-C able to do APE linking for real.
  c09c93d5d3b75ca0184eb9a3c326c3747d3dcdfe 2026-09-26 cosmo: fix aarch64 libc++ iostream - reserve x18/x28 in every pizlonated object
  3890863f9420cdf092b983f3bffdd0c17c72a4b6 2026-09-26 cosmo: --filc-fat-ape - single x86_64+aarch64 APE binaries (cosmocc-style double link + apelink)
  51f8f39557fe5d4ecfa8452ef1c66983cd737431 2026-09-26 cosmo: aarch64 Fil-C cosmo port (yolocosmo/libpas/usercosmo cross builds + driver support, qemu-verified)
  f5fc345b875f40e014b8d57e991ed8626cb4d91f 2026-09-26 cosmo: produce real APEs (apelink post-link) - every cosmo-mode link emits a Windows/macOS-runnable .com
  1636dbb63e6bdf76451c30b38743345114bbc5ba 2026-09-19 cosmo: libc++/libc++abi for the cosmo flavor (static) + C++ tests enabled
  298504fddcc003ea481e38eaece741af4c3c974f 2026-09-19 clang driver: cosmopolitan libc (cosmo) flavor - static-only links with cosmo crt/lds/libs

